<h1>linear hash</h1>
<p>
(algorithm)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A numeric function that maintains the order of input <a href="key.html"><em>keys</em></a> while changing their spacing.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Formal Definition:</strong> A <a href="hash.html"><em>hash function</em></a> f for keys in S such that k1, k2 &isin; S &and; k1 &gt; k2 &rarr; f(k1) &gt; f(k2).
</p>
<p>
<strong>Also known as</strong> order-preserving hash.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Generalization</strong> (I am a kind of ...)<br>
<a href="hash.html"><em>hash function</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Specialization</strong> (... is a kind of me.)<br>
<a href="orderPreservMinPerfectHash.html"><em>order-preserving minimal perfect hashing</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>Aggregate parent</strong> (I am a part of or used in ...)<br>
<a href="gridfile.html"><em>grid file</em></a>, <a href="hashheap.html"><em>hash heap</em></a>.
</p>
<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="linearHashing.html"><em>linear hashing</em></a>.
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

